{"chunk_id": "d4f48c2cd387", "text": "Krishna attempts to console Arjuna, who is shattered by the death of his son Abhimanyu. He reminds Arjuna that dying bravely in battle is the highest destiny of a Kshatriya and that Abhimanyu has earned heavenly reward through heroic combat. Still grieving, Arjuna demands to hear how his son was slain and bitterly reproaches his allies for failing to protect him. Yudhishthira explains that while Arjuna fought elsewhere, Drona formed a deadly battle array. Abhimanyu alone could break into it, and though the Pandavas tried to follow, Jayadratha blocked them by virtue of a boon. Surrounded by great warriors\u2014Drona, Karna, Kripa, and others\u2014the young hero fought fiercely, killing thousands before being overwhelmed and killed. Hearing this, Arjuna collapses in grief, then rises in fury and vows to kill Jayadratha the next day.\nKrishna consoles grieving Arjuna over Abhimanyu\u2019s death; Yudhishthira recounts the boy\u2019s heroic fall, and Arjuna vows to kill Jayadratha the next day.\nThemes: grief and consolation, warrior dharma, Abhimanyu's death, oath of vengeance, battlefield honor", "vector": [-0.0042563797906041145, -0.005237611476331949, -0.004223562311381102, 0.0049652294255793095, -0.00999609287828207, 0.029272865504026413, -0.006963791325688362, 0.008361800573766232, -0.012575517408549786, -0.01823318749666214, 0.018653247505426407, 0.005946461111307144, 0.015660326927900314, -0.00035421972279436886, -0.012319544330239296, 0.016671093180775642, 0.051693517714738846, -0.002873138291761279, 0.03544248268008232, -0.0176293533295393, -0.002751715015619993, 0.0019427731167525053, -0.0017688424559310079, 0.01833820343017578, -0.005211357492953539, 0.026450593024492264, -0.014439529739320278, -0.02458658069372177, 0.029850445687770844, -0.0181938074529171, -0.0017622789600864053, 0.004686283878982067, -0.0036098824348300695, 0.007206637877970934, -0.02332640439271927, 0.011886358261108398, 0.00011352670117048547, -0.024